# ⚠️ Required. SEC and the congressional disclosure sites want a User-Agent
# that identifies the caller. Rather than ship a placeholder — which would get
# you rate-limited with no clue why — the program refuses to start without it.
#
# This identifies **you** to those sites. It is sent nowhere else.
FZ_CONTACT="Your Name your@email.com"

# Optional: where local data lives (default ~/.floorzero)
# FZ_DATA_DIR="/path/to/data"

# Optional: enable FINRA sources (off-exchange short volume + the Darkpool section).
# ⚠️ **Off by default, deliberately.** FINRA's Terms of Use permit "ONLY your own
#    non-commercial personal or professional use", and restriction (d) forbids
#    developing a database from their data — which is what downloading into SQLite is.
#    The terms are reproduced verbatim in the UI; the judgement is yours, not ours.
#    While off: Shorts still runs on SEC fails-to-deliver; Darkpool shows only the terms.
